'''''Amaranthus polygonoides''''' is a species of [[flowering plant]] in the family [[Amaranthaceae]]. It is an annual native to Mexico, northern Central America, the Caribbean, the [[Galápagos]], and portions of the south-central and southeastern United States.<ref name = powo/> It goes by the common name of '''tropical amaranth'''.

==Subdivisions==
Three subdivisions are accepted:<ref name = powo/>
*''Amaranthus polygonoides'' var. ''berlandieri'' {{small|(Moq.) Iamonico}} – south-central United States to Honduras
*''Amaranthus polygonoides'' subsp. ''polygonoides'' – Caribbean, Florida, South Carolina, and Texas
*''Amaranthus polygonoides'' subsp. ''urceolatus'' {{small|(Andersson) Iamonico}} – Galápagos

